        "body": "iOS silently drops data-only FCM messages when the app is killed unless the APNS payload includes `content_available: 1` and `mutable_content: 1`. The Notification Service Extension needs these to wake up.\n\n## Fix\nIn `src/event_handler.rs` `create_fcm_payload()`, change `apns: None` to use `ApnsConfig` with `Aps { content_available: Some(ContentAvailable::On), mutable_content: Some(MutableContent::On) }`.\n\nThe `firebase-messaging-rs` crate already has full support: `ApnsConfig`, `Aps`, `ContentAvailable::On`, `MutableContent::On` are all available in `firebase_messaging_rs::fcm::ios`.\n\nAlso update `fcm_sender.rs` Message construction to pass `payload.apns` instead of `None`.\n\n## Files to change\n- `src/event_handler.rs` (create_fcm_payload, line ~779-785)\n- `src/fcm_sender.rs` (send_single, line ~148-157, pass payload.apns)\n- `src/models.rs` (FcmPayload already has `apns: Option<serde_json::Value>` but should use `Option<ApnsConfig>` from the crate)",
