        "body": "Closes #16\n\n## Problem\n\nData-only FCM messages (no `notification` field) are silently dropped on iOS when the app is killed or suspended. Without `content-available` and `mutable-content` in the APNS payload, iOS has no reason to wake the app or route the notification through the Notification Service Extension.\n\n## Why this approach\n\nThe root cause is that `Message::Token` was constructed with `apns: None` in `RealFcmClient::send_single()` — the single point where Firebase messages are built. Fixing it here means every outgoing message automatically gets the correct APNS config, with no opt-in required per notification type.\n\nAPNS config was placed in `fcm_sender.rs` (transport layer) rather than in `FcmPayload`/`event_handler.rs` because: (1) all our messages need these flags, (2) the typed `ApnsConfig` API from `firebase-messaging-rs` is cleaner than the `serde_json::Value` that `FcmPayload.apns` uses, and (3) it keeps event handling decoupled from iOS delivery mechanics.\n\nTwo code paths based on message content:\n- **Alert path** — messages with title/body get a `RichAlert` in `aps.alert`, plus `content-available: 1` and `mutable-content: 1`, with `apns-push-type: alert` and priority 10. Title/body are filtered from custom data to avoid duplication with `aps.alert`.\n- **Background path** — data-only messages without title/body use `ios_background_notification()` which sets `content-available: 1` with background push type and priority 5.\n\nA `debug_assert!` guards against future code accidentally setting `FcmPayload.apns`, enforcing that APNS config is transport-owned.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\n- **Android unaffected** — FCM ignores the `apns` field for Android devices.\n- **Requires iOS Notification Service Extension** — the diVine iOS app must have one to leverage `mutable-content`. Assumed already in place.\n- **No per-message opt-out** — every message gets the APNS override. Intentional since all messages are data-only and need background delivery.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `test_build_apns_config_creates_alert_payload_from_data_only_message` — verifies alert path JSON structure\n- `test_build_apns_config_uses_background_transport_without_alert_fields` — verifies background path JSON structure\n- All existing tests pass, clippy clean",
