        "body": "The core APNS fix looks right, and I think the transport-level placement in `fcm_sender.rs` is the correct direction. I’d like one small follow-up before merge for two reasons:\n\n1. `FcmPayload.apns` is now effectively ignored. `build_apns_config()` constructs APNS config from scratch and `send_single()` always uses that result, while the payload model still exposes an `apns` field. Nothing in this repo sets `payload.apns` today, so this is not a live bug, but it is a latent footgun and makes the model misleading. At minimum, please add a `debug_assert!(payload.apns.is_none())` plus a short comment explaining that APNS is transport-owned here. Longer-term, we may want to remove `apns` from `FcmPayload` entirely.\n\n2. In the alert path, `title` and `body` are currently duplicated: once in `aps.alert` and again as top-level APNS custom data because the full `data` map is passed into `ApnsConfig::new()`. That is probably harmless, but it adds bytes and makes the payload contract a bit muddier for any Notification Service Extension. Please filter `title` and `body` out of the custom APNS data before building the alert payload.\n\nThe dead `// Removed unused imports` comment can also be cleaned up while you’re in there, but I don’t consider that blocking.",
